[{"id":"VRCE-2-105-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":1,"english":"Then taking the pair of sandals on his head, Bharata in company with Śatrughna well pleased, ascended the car.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.821,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a02d028f1f23df8208d0a0423e9a274e5f6d764a2e8dcb9972edbe1753e69fda","compact":"db3ba10708b51423e9f7f61da6196e12e889b66ff23aca0dbd08e65fccb42434","nasal":"db3ba10708b51423e9f7f61da6196e12e889b66ff23aca0dbd08e65fccb42434"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":2,"english":"And Vasiştha, and Vāmadeva and Jāvāli steady his vow as well as the minister, honoured on account of their counsels, went before.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e8276b5c68941c991c12925dff1c5321acf1d7740dba6748183764867f828fd3","compact":"a17bc900cdf2c671b925a42b64ff939f5aea8079216074ca2589a901329f95b1","nasal":"f7ffb8d88795839384c9ee33c02c927ad00242195df86e249f4f6b1cbb87c188"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":3,"english":"And going round the charming Mandākinī, they went eastwards, circumambulating (at the same time) the mighty hill, Citrakuta.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.838,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9796d6d61bcfce773d6d2f614ac2d663aa15db2c5c0220dabd4d7306dce4176f","compact":"7045b3f7d87159a2ea0f1450f7273e54f5ae408169345400ef0ce26c2643df