r":"2105012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aa22696db9f738173d8ead274e9614b3be20589a44cbe67bd6d99e0d9344574d","compact":"9dbd5055a778f39e463c73680e3bc6365879ab59b2742aae2d089dc142d5ecc3","nasal":"9dbd5055a778f39e463c73680e3bc6365879ab59b2742aae2d089dc142d5ecc3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":13,"english":"Thus addressed by Vasiştha, Rāghava facing the east, conferred on me his sandals decked in gold, in order that I mighty carry on the government of the kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dba55c725b43db194571a4f0e3ce64d594fec1e16f10e3b1b4d029ecdf2b02eb","compact":"71de1ba02f5be2088065a55c40c353513f04db2f0f2704b0c6ec28570f6d5506","nasal":"71de1ba02f5be2088065a55c40c353513f04db2f0f2704b0c6ec28570f6d5506"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":14,"english":"Commanded by the magnanimous Rāma, I retrace my steps. I will go to Ayodhyā, taking the sandals along with me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0b63babf9cd051c1be82f5c31bac774c3fc9c076d92e74bab7615f243f2ff881","compact":"d4c3b661c03ec4826365550480cf163c35ecb4533ea7f04c1924cfff917f47e8","nasal":"d4c3b661c03ec4826365550480cf163c35ecb4533ea7f04c1924cfff917f47e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":15,"english":"Hearing these auspicious words of the highsouled Bharata, the ascetic Bharadvāja said to Bharata.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af7c384dc1123ee1140c87c33c0945312d2c76173f19502795d850e7560f2e74","compact":"0d1ec7bf8b9ec0f525787764e3fc1804547d1113f82ee52462b478ce19f6e76b","nasal":"0d1ec7bf8b9ec0f525787764e3fc1804547d1113f82ee52462b478ce19f6e76b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":16,"english":"It is no wonder that Rāma has acted nobly by you, foremost among men and possessed of an (excellent) character and disposition, even as water poured out, flow downwards.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.623,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"72b7e8d917e8a3f121400f9663239a93f0518b57c6f4d18649bd66dcb9304ade","compact":"d757deb152061f2329e2cd9bf75c9348981c32447e9ea267a6a850cf7f409fda","nasal":"d757deb152061f2329e2cd9bf75c9348981c32447e9ea267a6a850cf7f409fda"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":17,"english":"Your father Dasaratha has become freed from his debts, since he has a son like to you, righteous and attached to virtue.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.93,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65400af63981c4886558f85988cda3225aae305c89040521e7fc7e24175053be","compact":"1e39e59afa1624529bf663bedae84c1c44856d3ea76805e71973686859a4e5fc","nasal":"1e39e59afa1624529bf663bedae84c1c44856d3ea76805e71973686859a4e5fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":18,"english":"When the ascetic had said this, Bharata with joined palms paid his respects to that highly wise one, by taking hold of his feet.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"72b85f7e41ce16725e8db8a7864408cf69badc3b7aaf71a8c7f223de6def8caf","compact":"525ad7db5276331f680ee561a87fedd8aba92406f28f761b5e5d492bd440f875","nasal":"447d4db33848450d3e5e68a85b876d20414494cb865c05b954f07c0b10e37048"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":19,"english":"And after having again and again gone round Bharadvāja, the graceful Bharata went to Ayodhyā accompanied by his counsellors.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bbc0113e576a7e5cfa2e10d5d308c056d0d610d70bfc3ad65b7b2dfe322f84f1","compact":"1f1b62e10f67cc22625e4f8d6ee8965b001eebc197f717efdc862b995676c69c","nasal":"4543e7b41425d3a25105134e1043d2ee1bb89717fc8330267373e9f1c156e2d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":20,"english":"And returning by means of cars and carts, horses and elephants, that army marching in the wake of Bharata, spread wide.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"285f05c0717320be70bc4eb007bb30a188601a2e72e70dd8a8982fc7964ee635","compact":"9e6935604fd8be01092c80c10c4c349c6323e799f0638f8942fe4567c8a350a0","nasal":"9e6935604fd8be01092c80c10c4c349c6323e799f0638f8942fe4567c8a350a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":21,"english":"And after having crossed the beautiful river Yamunā flowing in waves, they again beheld the river Gangā of auspicious waters.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5b9c579d5f87d3b52ff620470f48f7861187fc977430e8df13c8a5cee9468473","compact":"e96338d63e107ec0702bca6e2c4a28b393643ae1061bff11c441de8406124e92","nasal":"c1b1bc95b4b89bf2a772a57b6243ffff7570638c11681c7d21499d8ae5bb659b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":22,"english":"And having along with his friend crossed over that river filled with beautiful waters, Bharata together with his army entered the charming city of Srigavera.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"858142649fb60a681f48ba2198b98d8bb72d8ff1de131ed997533647ba84efb6","compact":"b94204f54d0f8c51710a2dad5e6dadd93fa8c0c0a2e20eb822bc31e8eb606bdb","nasal":"00e3e15f06d2da2a3e10ee397d36497b9521f761f09816421123cb56105427f5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-105-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":105,"verse":23,"english":"And from the city of Śộngava he went to Ayodhyā and again beheld it. And seeing Ayodhyā bereft of his father and mother, Bharata burning in grief, said to the charioteer.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.897,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-113-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2105023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7886d87c852ce28b8c4af5af4131d121055926f132d6363bdd5de006e02a48b5","compact":"3c3